      en: "Valencia is a notable site on the Caribbean island of Trinidad. A growing village at the crossroads of major roads in northeastern Trinidad. Its setting reflects both the geographical diversity and the cultural heritage of the island. Notably: Important transport junction. Another point of interest: Surrounded by forests and quarries. For students, the location offers a concrete bridge between curriculum content and the real world. Geography K7 — island geography and cultural heritage."
