      en: "Freeport is a notable site on the Caribbean island of Trinidad. A town in central Trinidad with a mix of agricultural and residential areas. Its setting reflects both the geographical diversity and the cultural heritage of the island. Notably: Agricultural center. Another point of interest: Near the Solomon Hochoy Highway. For students, the location offers a concrete bridge between curriculum content and the real world. Geography K7 — island geography and cultural heritage."
