      en: "Debe is a notable site on the Caribbean island of Trinidad. Known for its wide array of Indian delicacies and street food, especially doubles. Its setting reflects both the geographical diversity and the cultural heritage of the island. Notably: Street food capital. Another point of interest: Famous for 'doubles'. For students, the location offers a concrete bridge between curriculum content and the real world. Geography K7 — island geography and cultural heritage."
