      en: "Arouca is a notable site on the Caribbean island of Trinidad. A historic town in the East-West Corridor, originally founded as a Spanish mission. Its setting reflects both the geographical diversity and the cultural heritage of the island. Notably: Former Spanish mission. Another point of interest: Part of the East-West Corridor. For students, the location offers a concrete bridge between curriculum content and the real world. Geography K7 — island geography and cultural heritage."
